  "verbalization": "Taxodone is associated with HCC1937 through its interaction with Leukocyte antigen CD37, which serves as a target for multiple structurally diverse compounds. These compounds, including [(1R,2R,6R,10S,11R,13S,14R,15R)-13-acetyloxy-1,14-dihydroxy-4,12,12,15-tetramethyl-5-oxo-8-tetracyclo[8.5.0.02,6.011,13]pentadeca-3,8-dienyl]methyl (9Z,12Z)-octadeca-9,12-dienoate and its enantiomer, are all identified as targets of Leukocyte antigen CD37. The shared mechanism of action involves binding to CD37, suggesting a potential for Taxodone to exert similar effects through a similar molecular interaction. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Taxodone and HCC1937 via the CD37 pathway, with the structural diversity of the targets indicating a broad range of potential mechanisms. The consistent association across the three paths highlights the importance of CD37 as a key mediator in this relationship.",
